# Cursor Rules — Focused / Edi Backend

## Tech Stack
- Node.js (18+)
- Express.js
- MongoDB (Mongoose)
- JWT Authentication
- bcrypt for password hashing
- Docker & Docker Compose

## Architecture Rules
- REST APIs only (no GraphQL)
- Role-based access control (RBAC)
- Platform-Admin APIs must be isolated under `/api/platform-admin`
- No direct DB access from routes (service layer mandatory)
- Controllers must be thin
- Business rules must live in services

## Roles
- SUPER_ADMIN (Platform Admin)
- OPERATIONS_ADMIN
- FACULTY
- STUDENT

## Security Rules
- All write APIs require authentication
- SUPER_ADMIN actions must be audit logged
- Passwords must never be returned in responses
- JWT expiry: 24h (access), refresh-token optional

## Database Rules
- MongoDB via Mongoose
- No hard dependency on MongoDB-specific operators in services
- Schema design must support DB replacement

## AI Guardrails
- No AI prompts or OpenAI logic in Platform-Admin services
- AI is a downstream consumer of syllabus metadata only

## Naming Conventions
- kebab-case for routes
- camelCase for variables
- PascalCase for models

## Versioning
- APIs must be versioned: `/api/v1/...`
